w an adapter hands the SDK that steering wheel; the renderer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"prefers it over its own controller whenever the content adapter conforms.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"All three members are called on the main thread (the renderer is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"@MainActor","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"); the change handler must likewise be invoked on the main"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"thread, for every transition — including viewer-driven ones (the system UI"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"can dismiss the window at any time), which is the whole reason the handler"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"exists: the break format follows what is actually on screen."}]}]}],"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/optiviewadscore\/pictureinpicturecapable"]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"OptiViewAdsCore"}],"symbolKind":"protocol","title":"PictureInPictureCapable","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PictureInPictureCapable"}],"roleHeading":"Protocol","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PictureInPictureCapable"}],"externalID":"s:15OptiViewAdsCore09PictureInE7CapableP"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore/documentation/OptiViewAdsCore/PictureInPictureCapable/onPictureInPictureChange(_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/optiviewadscore.OptiViewAdsCore\/documentation\/OptiViewAdsCore\/PictureInPictureCapable\/onPictureInPictureChange(_:)","title":"onPictureInPictureChange(_:)","required":true,"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"onPictureInPictureChange","kind":"identif